# Agent rules — `@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-web-sdk`

This package is a Svelte SDK published to GitHub Packages. Consumers
add it as `pnpm add @mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-web-sdk` and import components
directly.

## Conventions

* **Svelte 5 runes only**: `$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`,
  `$props`. No legacy reactive syntax.
* **UI primitives**: always from `@mssfoobar/ui`. Never hand-roll a
  `<button>`, `<input>`, dialog, etc. with raw Tailwind.
* **Auth / HTTP**: consumers pass a `getToken` callback or auth
  adapter to the SDK's provider component. The SDK doesn't read
  cookies, doesn't call Keycloak directly, doesn't import host-app
  internals.
* **No host-app coupling**: do not import from `$lib/aoh/...` or any
  consumer-app path. The SDK is self-contained.

## Workspace dependencies

* `@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-client` (workspace:*) — the wire layer
* `@mssfoobar/__AOH_MODULE_NAME__-types` (workspace:*) — DTOs (typically transitive)
* `@mssfoobar/ui` (workspace:*) — UI primitives
* `@mssfoobar/logger` (workspace:*) — structured logging

All four are declared as **peerDependencies**. The consumer's
workspace provides them; we don't bundle them.

## Per-subpath exports

Each user-facing component gets its own `exports` entry in
`package.json` so consumers can tree-shake. See `modules/gis/web`'s
`package.json` (published as `@mssfoobar/gis-web-sdk`) for the worked-out
pattern (one entry per component directory under
`sdk/components/<Name>/index.svelte`).
